<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE starship-flight-15 ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Starship Flight 15 / Starlink Group 31-2 (OLP-2, Starbase) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
TIMELINE mode: every ignition/cutoff/separation/fairing time is a published hard event; mdot=F_vac/(Isp_vac*g0); thrust SL/vac on ambient pressure.
FITTED (least squares vs published knots): vertical rise 12.23 s, kick 0.512 deg over 10 s, Cd 0.400, payload 78898 kg,
gravity turn, then linear-tangent steering tan(theta)=0.0324--0.000486*(t-t_ign stage 1).
Vehicle config: SpaceX Starship V3 (Super Heavy 33×Raptor 3 + Ship 3 SL + 3 vac Raptor 3) — TIMELINE mode (sim/vehicles/starship_v3.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
Starship V3: Super Heavy 3,650 t propellant, 33× Raptor 3, 80.8 MN / 8,240 tf liftoff; Ship Block 3 1,600 t propellant, 1,600 tf initial thrust (Wikipedia citing SpaceX &#x27;Introducing Starship V3&#x27; / technical specifications, 12 May 2026). V3 dry masses and Raptor 3 Isp are ASSUMED (see fields).
TIMELINE mode uses SpaceX&#x27;s published Flight 15 event times (content.spacex.com/api/spacex-website/missions/starship-flight-15, also spacex.com/launches/starship-flight-15): MECO 139 s, hot-stage / ship ignition 141 s, ship ascent cutoff 489 s. Boostback and catch are not modelled; unburned booster propellant stands in for the recovery reserve.
The 20 s orbital insertion burn (T+26:10–26:30) and payload deploy (start 35:01, complete 1:17:40) are flown in post_cutoff. SpaceX: ~275 km, ~14 orbits, &gt;22-hour flight, then RTLS catch if the vehicle is healthy.
PRE-FLIGHT ILLUSTRATIVE. Starship Flight 15 / Starlink Group 31-2, 26 V3 sats, OLP-2 Starbase, T0 2026-11-13T22:45:00Z (Fri Nov 13 2:45 p.m. PST), 75-minute window, LL2 TBC pending regulatory approval. First attempt to catch both Super Heavy V3 and the ship at the launch site.
Ascent event times are SpaceX&#x27;s published F15 timeline (MECO 139 s, hot-stage 141 s, ship cutoff 489 s). The 20 s orbital insertion burn (26:10–26:30) is flown post-cutoff; payload deploy start 35:01, complete 1:17:40. Ship is then scheduled to fly ~14 orbits and attempt RTLS catch (deorbit T+21:35:57) — deorbit/catch are not in this file, which ends at deploy complete.
Target (see launch config): insertion 180 km, apoapsis 275 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 107.53 deg; payload 78898 kg.
Pad: 25.996770N -97.157990E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-11-13T22:45:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: after final cutoff T+489.0 s the stage coasts (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model) to PAYLOAD DEPLOY T+4660 s; rows tagged -coast/-burn.
POST-CUTOFF burn &#x27;Orbital insertion burn&#x27;: ign T+1570.0 s, 12.8 s at 2451.66 kN prograde (Isp 350 s); Open-loop: ASSUMED single Raptor 3 SL (2,451,663 N, F14 analog) for the residual-limited duration 12.80 s (published 20 s cannot be completed: constant 1,600 tf / 350 s leaves only 9143 kg). Not solved to a perigee target. The impulse still exceeds a 180×275 km circularization (~26 m/s); residuals are reported, not hidden.
POST-CUTOFF deploy T+4660 s (SpaceX Flight 15 timeline: deploy start T+00:35:01, complete T+01:17:40): alt 755.03 km, osculating 202.5 x 771.6 km, i 31.185 deg.
POST-CUTOFF note: SpaceX target altitude ~275 km after the insertion burn. A 20 s / 1×250 tf burn is ~236 m/s at this cutoff mass, vs ~26 m/s to circularize a 180×275 km transfer; the residual-limited ~13 s burn is still ~150 m/s. The resulting orbit is not expected to be 275 km circular. Residuals are reported, not hidden.
POST-CUTOFF note: Ship residual propellant after a constant 1,600 tf / 350 s, 348 s ascent is 9.14 t, short of the 14.3 t a published 20 s insertion would need. Insertion is flown residual-limited. 1,600 tf is published as initial thrust (SpaceX via Wikipedia).
POST-CUTOFF note: Deorbit burn T+21:35:57 and ship catch T+22:32:34 (SpaceX F15 timeline) are not modelled; file ends at deploy complete T+01:17:40.</description>
